CM ============================================================
CM  phased_array_4el_rdf.nec — TM-ADF-NEC-004 Rev A
CM  4-Element Switched Phased Array for HF RDF, 40-meter band
CM  Frequency: 7.15 MHz
CM  Array: 4 λ/4 verticals in square, λ/4 spacing per side
CM
CM  Geometry:
CM    Element spacing: 10.5m (λ/4 at 7.15 MHz)
CM    E1 (NW): (-5.25, +5.25, 0)–(-5.25, +5.25, 10.15)
CM    E2 (NE): (+5.25, +5.25, 0)–(+5.25, +5.25, 10.15)
CM    E3 (SE): (+5.25, -5.25, 0)–(+5.25, -5.25, 10.15)
CM    E4 (SW): (-5.25, -5.25, 0)–(-5.25, -5.25, 10.15)
CM
CM  Phased feed for NORTH BEAM:
CM    E1(NW): 0° phase, magnitude 1.0
CM    E2(NE): 90° phase, magnitude 1.0
CM    E3(SE): 180° phase, magnitude 1.0
CM    E4(SW): 270° phase, magnitude 1.0
CM  (Sequential phase around array = endfire toward North)
CM
CM  This model: NORTH BEAM phasing
CM  Expected: cardioid pattern, peak North, null South
CM  F/B ratio: expect 10–15 dB
CM ============================================================
CM
CM E1 (Northwest element): tag 1
CM E2 (Northeast element): tag 2
CM E3 (Southeast element): tag 3
CM E4 (Southwest element): tag 4
CM
CM End geometry, real ground
CM
CM Average ground (σ=0.005 S/m, ε=13)
CM
CM Frequency: 7.15 MHz
CM
CM ── NORTH BEAM PHASING ─────────────────────────────────────
CM E1: 0° phase = (1.0 + j0.0)
CM E2: 90° phase = (0.0 - j1.0) = rotate 90° CW
CM E3: 180° phase = (-1.0 + j0.0)
CM E4: 270° phase = (0.0 + j1.0)
CM
CM Azimuth radiation pattern (elevation=10°, azimuth 0–360°, 5°)
CM
CM Elevation pattern (azimuth=0°/North, elevation 0–90°, 2°)
CM
CM ============================================================
CM  TO MODEL EAST BEAM: change phasing to:
CM    E1: 270° = EX 0 1 1 0  0.0 1.0
CM    E2:   0° = EX 0 2 1 0  1.0 0.0
CM    E3:  90° = EX 0 3 1 0  0.0 -1.0
CM    E4: 180° = EX 0 4 1 0 -1.0 0.0
CM
CM  FOR RDF BEARING MEASUREMENT:
CM    1. Run model for N, E, S, W beams (4 separate runs)
CM    2. Record peak gain direction and F/B ratio for each
CM    3. In field: compare RSSI on all 4 beams simultaneously
CM    4. Bearing = direction of highest RSSI (peak beam pointing toward Tx)
CM    5. Gaussian interpolation between beam peaks for sub-step accuracy
CM
CM  MUTUAL COUPLING EFFECTS:
CM    With 4 elements at λ/4 spacing, mutual impedance is significant.
CM    NEC-2 accounts for this automatically via method-of-moments.
CM    Expect: driven element Z ≈ 36+j21Ω (vs. isolated monopole 36+j21Ω)
CM    Detuning due to mutual coupling: 5–15% change in beam peak direction.
CM    Calibrate by measuring actual RSSI vs. bearing angle in field.
CM ============================================================
